language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ All-interval series of size n: the pitch classes 0 to n-1 are each used once in a series x, and the intervals between neighbouring pitch classes are all different and cover 1 to n-1.
given n : int(2..30)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..n-1)
find diffs : matrix indexed by [int(1..n-1)] of int(1..n-1)

branching on [x]

such that
$ each pitch class occurs exactly once in the series
allDiff(x),
$ each interval is the distance between a pair of neighbouring pitch classes
forAll i : int(1..n-1) . ((diffs[i] = x[i+1] - x[i]) \/ (diffs[i] = x[i] - x[i+1])),
$ the intervals are all different, so they cover every interval from 1 to n-1
allDiff(diffs)
